8.	List the total number of projects that have employee(s) who work on it make less than $50k. (Hint: You need to use keyword DISTINCT in this query. Can you tell me why?).

Select count(distinct(p.pid)) as "Total Number Of Projects"
from project p
join workon w on p.pid = w.pid
join employee e on w.empid = e.empid
where e.salary < 50000

Total Number Of Projects
6

Keyword "DISTINCT" ensures that each project is counted only once, regardless of how many employees working on it earn < $50,000



